{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat ../research.json'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"audit_spec_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-06_19-22-21-hashicorp_raft-real-run/audit-spec/v1.json\",\n  \"audit_spec_version\": 1,\n  \"activity_roles\": {\n    \"A1\": {\n      \"role\": \"core\",\n      \"relation\": \"Qualified support for decision formation and legal advancement\"\n    },\n    \"A2\": {\n      \"role\": \"core\",\n      \"relation\": \"Context validity and acquisition, transfer or loss of authority\"\n    },\n    \"A3\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Recovery and resynchronization of eligible participation\"\n    },\n    \"A4\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Configuration and participant eligibility\"\n    },\n    \"A5\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Decision application and consumption\"\n    },\n    \"A6\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"History, persistence and reconstruction of support\"\n    },\n    \"A7\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Client contracts, invocation intervals and observed completion\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"activity_focus\": [],\n  \"understanding_status\": \"usable\",\n  \"core_overview\": {\n    \"formation\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"The elected leader stamps and persists commands, then reports its local match and notifies peer replicators. Sender-bounded AppendEntries and snapshot success report matching indexes to a tenure-local commitment object, which includes only latest-configuration voters. Its majority order statistic advances only through the current-term startIndex. A main-loop notification consumes that index, commits membership and enqueues ordered FSM work; follower append handling propagates leader commitment after prefix checks and conflict replacement. runFSM resolves command futures after callbacks, while log dispatch watermarks precede callback completion.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-replicate\",\n        \"B-quorum\",\n        \"B-commit-consume\",\n        \"B-fsm\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-quorum-index\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"M-apply\",\n        \"M-commit\",\n        \"M-consume\",\n        \"M-follower\",\n        \"M-fsm\",\n        \"M-fsm-rest\",\n        \"M-leader\",\n        \"M-leader-loop\",\n        \"M-reply\",\n        \"M-send\",\n        \"M-snapshot-send\",\n        \"M-update\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"context\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"Normal timeout candidacy requires local voter eligibility. Optional pre-vote precedes term persistence, self-vote and requests only to voters. Recipients enforce candidate membership, term, prior vote and last-log freshness; request-specific response channels and majority tally acquire leadership. Transfers catch up a target then send TimeoutNow, whose election bypasses pre-vote/known-leader rejection but still tallies votes. Incoming qualifying terms, higher-term replication replies, lease loss and committed self-removal end a tenure. Old replication callbacks retain old commitment/stepDown objects; cleanup stops workers, fails remaining inflight/verification futures and discards tenure fields. Already queued FSM work can still complete. Network heartbeat fast-path carries no entries or commitment and may run concurrently.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-election\",\n        \"B-tenure\",\n        \"B-transfer\",\n        \"B-transport\",\n        \"B-verify-start\",\n        \"B-verify-support\",\n        \"B-verify-finish\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-verify-support\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"M-durable\",\n        \"M-elect-send\",\n        \"M-election\",\n        \"M-follower\",\n        \"M-follower-loop\",\n        \"M-heartbeat\",\n        \"M-leader\",\n        \"M-leader-loop\",\n        \"M-lease\",\n        \"M-net-dispatch\",\n        \"M-notify\",\n        \"M-prevote\",\n        \"M-prevote-send\",\n        \"M-snapshot-send\",\n        \"M-timeout-now\",\n        \"M-transfer\",\n        \"M-transport\",\n        \"M-update\",\n        \"M-verify\",\n        \"M-verify-vote\",\n        \"M-vote\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"connection\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"Persistent vote/term and log freshness constrain subsequent authority acquisition; durable log entries survive tenure loss although their uncommitted futures fail. Each new leader resets volatile match evidence and appends a current-term noop before advancing old-history commitment. Configuration admission waits for both stable membership and current-term commitment, then changes the support electorate; suffix replacement can roll latest membership back. Snapshot capture includes applied history plus committed configuration, and restart/install reconstruct history and membership before participation/catch-up. Verification is a separate authority-support path: its threshold counts voters, but notification registration spans all replicators. That discrepancy is retained without equating callback count with legitimate authority.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-election\",\n        \"B-tenure\",\n        \"B-membership\",\n        \"B-history\",\n        \"B-resync\",\n        \"B-quorum\",\n        \"B-verify-start\",\n        \"B-verify-support\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-quorum-index\",\n        \"F-verify-support\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"M-apply\",\n        \"M-commit\",\n        \"M-durable\",\n        \"M-elect-send\",\n        \"M-election\",\n        \"M-follower\",\n        \"M-follower-loop\",\n        \"M-fsm-rest\",\n        \"M-heartbeat\",\n        \"M-install\",\n        \"M-leader\",\n        \"M-leader-loop\",\n        \"M-lease\",\n        \"M-notify\",\n        \"M-prevote\",\n        \"M-prevote-send\",\n        \"M-restart\",\n        \"M-snapshot-build\",\n        \"M-snapshot-send\",\n        \"M-suffrage\",\n        \"M-update\",\n        \"M-verify\",\n        \"M-verify-vote\",\n        \"M-vote\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"open_details\": [\n      \"Verification eligibility and callback timing relative to election/lease expiry.\",\n      \"Legal sender history for follower commitment beyond the current validated request prefix.\",\n      \"Partial-store-error recovery after conflict truncation; delayed snapshots; manual Restore and forced RecoverCluster paths.\",\n      \"Transport-specific pipeline ordering and error behavior beyond representative dispatch.\"\n    ],\n    \"core_gaps\": [],\n    \"status\": \"usable\",\n    \"rationale\": \"Representative formation, authority transition, old-work handling and necessary membership/recovery/application support have been traced. Local discrepancies and deeper variants remain explicitly open.\"\n  },\n  \"understanding_changes\": [\n    {\n      \"operation_id\": \"c9b90256572541038c4b6ffda0cd9000\",\n      \"version\": 1,\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"selections\",\n        \"match\": {\n          \"operation_id\": \"c9b90256572541038c4b6ffda0cd9000\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"next_objective\": {\n    \"action\": \"investigate_and_refocus\",\n    \"boundary\": \"both_core_paths\",\n    \"reason\": \"Use results to update understanding and compare the remaining frontier\",\n    \"core_gaps\": []\n  },\n  \"drafts\": [],\n  \"candidates\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"324bee1b720648a6af48200af143e19a\",\n      \"question\": {\n        \"audit_spec_version\": 1,\n        \"disposition\": \"concrete_suspicion\",\n        \"preferred_check\": \"controlled_schedule\",\n        \"question\": \"Can VerifyLeader consume successful notifications from nonvoters as sufficient authority support, and thereby return success when the local peer can no longer safely serve the API’s promised leadership check?\",\n        \"importance\": \"Incorrect success can authorize stale FSM reads after another voter majority acquires authority; the local eligibility/accounting discrepancy matters even before a wider read witness is constructed.\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"M-apply\",\n          \"M-client\",\n          \"M-commit\",\n          \"M-durable\",\n          \"M-elect-send\",\n          \"M-election\",\n          \"M-follower\",\n          \"M-follower-loop\",\n          \"M-future\",\n          \"M-heartbeat\",\n          \"M-leader\",\n          \"M-leader-loop\",\n          \"M-lease\",\n          \"M-notify\",\n          \"M-prevote\",\n          \"M-prevote-send\",\n          \"M-shutdown\",\n          \"M-snapshot-send\",\n          \"M-suffrage\",\n          \"M-update\",\n          \"M-verify\",\n          \"M-verify-api\",\n          \"M-verify-vote\",\n          \"M-vote\"\n        ],\n        \"participants\": [\n          \"leader\",\n          \"voting followers\",\n          \"nonvoting replication peers\",\n          \"VerifyLeader caller\"\n        ],\n        \"objects\": [\n          \"verifyFuture\",\n          \"replication notify maps\",\n          \"configuration electorate\"\n        ],\n        \"contexts\": [\n          \"Established leadership with mixed voter/nonvoter membership\",\n          \"Verification interval with unavailable voter responses\"\n        ],\n        \"event_paths\": [\n          \"VerifyLeader -> verifyCh -> verifyLeader -> all replication notify maps -> heartbeat/append/snapshot response -> notifyAll -> vote -> verifyCh -> leaderLoop result\"\n        ],\n        \"activity_classes\": [\n          \"A2\"\n        ],\n        \"behavior_ids\": [\n          \"B-verify-start\",\n          \"B-verify-support\",\n          \"B-verify-finish\"\n        ],\n        \"fact_ids\": [\n          \"F-verify-support\"\n        ],\n        \"supporting_behavior_ids\": {\n          \"B-membership\": \